    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The change is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the direct level rules with a two-stage points \u2192 level system.\n\n**`MembershipLevelCalculator`** (`util/`) \u2014 reworked from computing a level directly to computing points first, then deriving the level:\n- `membershipPoints(owner)`: starts at 0, adds `+2` for a present email, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` for a household of 3+ (new `hasLargeHousehold` helper reading `Owner.householdSize`), and `+3` for tenure over 365 days.\n- `membershipLevel(owner)`: maps points to level via `min(4, 1 + points/2)`, which gives exactly 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n- The tenure/household predicates stay as small private single-responsibility helpers; magic numbers are named constants.\n\n**`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping alongside `membershipLevel`, each delegating to the calculator via a small `computeMembershipPoints`/`computeMembershipLevel` method (no logic duplicated in the mapper).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipPoints` schema field and updated `membershipLevel` (now max 4) with the new derivation description, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes both fields.\n\n**`OwnerAuditLogger`** \u2014 updated the renamed method call (`membershipLevel(owner)`), still logging the level.\n\nBoth fields are now returned; the acceptance test (fresh owner with email, no namesake \u2192 3 points, level 2) and the full suite pass.",
