    "probe_text": "Here is every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, in the order it happens. The endpoint is served by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:183`).\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Bean Validation on the request DTO** (`OwnerFieldsDto`, triggered by `@Valid`/`@Validated` on the `OwnersApi` interface). Failure \u2192 400:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words, apostrophe/hyphen/space separators), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (same, allows trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)` (optional, no `@NotNull`)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 no annotation (validated later in code)\n2. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")`.\n\n## Inside the controller body\n\n3. **Normalize address in-place** (`AddressNormalizer.normalize`) \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE abbreviations. *(side-effect: mutates the DTO)*\n4. **Required-field presence check** (`OwnerFieldsValidator.findMissingOrBlankFields`) for firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` if any missing/blank.\n5. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (`id`, `pets`, `householdId` ignored, so `isNew()==true`).\n6. **Load same-last-name owners** (case-insensitive read).\n7. **Set `namesakeCount`** (`NamesakeCounter` \u2014 count of matching first+last name). *(side-effect)*\n8. **Assign household** (`assignHousehold`): set `householdId` (SHA-256 of last name + postcode), compute household members (same last name + postcode), set `householdSize = members + 1`. *(side-effect)*\n9. **Normalize `telephone` to E.164** (`TelephoneNormalizer`) \u2014 invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`. *(side-effect + validation)*\n10. **Normalize `email`** (`EmailNormalizer`) \u2014 lower-case; invalid \u2192 `InvalidEmailException`. *(side-effect + validation)*\n11. **Disposable-email check** (`DisposableEmailDomainValidator`) \u2014 rejects mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n12. **Postcode/city check** (`PostcodeValidator`) \u2014 if present, must be 4 digits within the city's region range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n13. **Duplicate-identity check** (`rejectIfDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 loads same-telephone owners; matching `IdentityKey` (telephone|email|householdId) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n14. **Household rule** (`applyHouseholdRule`):\n    - No existing members \u2192 **flag possible duplicate** (`PossibleDuplicateDetector`): set `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`. *(side-effect)*\n    - Existing members and `sharesHousehold != true` \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException`; if opted in, clear the duplicate flags. *(side-effect)*\n15. **Registration-date validation** (`RegistrationDateValidator`) \u2014 future date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n16. **Default registration date** to `LocalDate.now()` if null. *(side-effect)*\n17. **Roll to next business day** if weekend (`BusinessDayResolver.toBusinessDay`). *(side-effect)*\n18. **Daily-limit check** \u2014 count owners registered that date; `>= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n19. **Set `bulkSignupWarning`** (`BulkSignupWarningEvaluator` \u2014 true when today's count > 80). *(side-effect)*\n20. **City-limit check** \u2014 count owners in the city; `>= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` \u2192 `CityOwnerLimitException`.\n21. **Set `customerCode`** (`CustomerCodeGenerator` \u2014 `REGION-<hash of telephone+lastName>`, region from `LocalityResolver`). *(side-effect)*\n22. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (JPA `persist`, IDENTITY id assigned) in its own `@Transactional`. **Entity-level constraints** enforced at persist/flush: `Owner.address`/`city`/`telephone` `@NotEmpty`, telephone `@Pattern` E.164, plus `Person` firstName/lastName `@NotEmpty`. *(side-effect: DB insert)*\n23. **Audit log** \u2014 `ownerAuditLogger.ownerCreated(owner)` writes one INFO line to the `AUDIT` SLF4J logger. *(side-effect \u2014 the only \"event\"; no DB write, no email, no ApplicationEvent)*\n24. **Map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`** (computes derived display/membership fields).\n25. **Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header** and return **201 Created**.\n\nTwo things worth flagging about the design:\n\n- **No `@Transactional` on `addOwner`.** Each read/count and the final save run in separate transactions, so the duplicate/limit checks (steps 13, 18, 20) are not atomic with the insert \u2014 concurrent requests can race past them.\n- **There are no JPA lifecycle callbacks** (`@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`), no `@EntityListeners`, and no `ApplicationEventPublisher` anywhere \u2014 every side-effect above is explicit in the controller flow."
